-- title:
--   Connectedness criterion for a finite flat model of ̄ V⊕̄ V
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field of characteristic $p$ with $p$ an odd prime, let $\mathbb{Z}_p$ be equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}_p \to \mathbb{Z}/p$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by $p$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V = 2$ together with a homomorphism $\bar\rho \colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{End}_k V$ trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume `ρbar.IsLocallyFlatCocycleAd p 0`: there are a commutative ring $H$ carrying a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}_p$, finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module, and a bijection $e$ from the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra homomorphisms $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ under convolution onto $V \times V$ which turns convolution into addition and intertwines the action of $\sigma \in \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ on points (post-composition by $\sigma$) with the diagonal action $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ on $V \times V$, the local group being mapped to the global one by restriction of scalars followed by restriction to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Then there is a $k$-subspace $V_0 \subseteq V$ such that: $V_0$ is stable under all $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ for $\sigma$ in the local group at $p$; $\bar\rho(\sigma)v - v \in V_0$ for every $v \in V$ and every $\sigma$ whose associated automorphism lies in the inertia subgroup of the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ (viewed inside the decomposition subgroup); and if $V_0 = V$ then such a Hopf algebra datum $(H,e)$ as above exists with, in addition, $(\mathbb{Z}/p) \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$ a local ring.
--
--   This is the connectedness criterion for finite flat models: the span of the inertia displacements on $\bar V \oplus \bar V$ detects, via the connected–étale sequence, whether the given finite flat Hopf algebra model can be taken with connected special fibre. It feeds into [`ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_or_connected_model_or_ordinary_of_isLocallyFlatCocycleAd`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_or_connected_model_or_ordinary_of_isLocallyFlatCocycleAd), the trichotomy used in the local analysis at $p$ of flat deformation conditions.
